~ (x, y) -> (-x, -y)#This choice applies the wrong sign, direction, or sequence step. Recheck the coordinate rule and transform each vertex in order.
~ (x, y) -> (-x, y)#This choice applies the wrong sign, direction, or sequence step. Recheck the coordinate rule and transform each vertex in order.
= (x, y) -> (y, -x)#Correct. This applies the transformation rule in the required order and gives the image coordinate.
}

::GEO_U02_L04_Q13::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L04_Q13<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.5<br><br>Question:<br>When drawing a polygon image, why must every vertex be transformed? {
= The image is formed by the transformed vertices#Correct. This applies the transformation rule in the required order and gives the image coordinate.
