::GEO_U02_L04_Q16::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U02_L04_Q16<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.CGM.5<br><br>Question:<br>Which action should come first when drawing an image from a sequence? {
~ Connect random points that look correct#This choice applies the wrong sign, direction, or sequence step. Recheck the coordinate rule and transform each vertex in order.
~ Skip intermediate coordinates#This choice applies the wrong sign, direction, or sequence step. Recheck the coordinate rule and transform each vertex in order.
~ Graph the final figure before calculating points#This choice applies the wrong sign, direction, or sequence step. Recheck the coordinate rule and transform each vertex in order.
= Apply the first transformation to the original vertices#Correct. This applies the transformation rule in the required order and gives the image coordinate.
}

